The attached image shows flow cytometry histograms illustrating the effect of Nano-11 on the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells (DCs). DCs incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) for two days show a marked increase in CD80 and CD86 expression compared to the medium control (gray line), indicated by the rightward shift of the peaks. A slight increase in CD40 expression is also observed. This enhanced expression of costimulatory molecules signifies DC activation, which, as stated in the PDF, is a critical step in initiating an effective immune response, highlighting Nano-11's role as a potent vaccine adjuvant.